abstract: >-
  An AI-assisted research loop examined the physics claims in the Pais patents and related propulsion
  and superconductivity claims. Over eleven runs it logged 162 searches with sources, built a ledger of
  36 settled results and a 40-page mathematics run sheet, and stopped by its own rule. Nothing in the
  patents survives as physics; what survives is engineering (a magnetically held rotor and a light-driven
  film in a laser cavity), plus two claims that only null tests can settle. This record sets out five
  deciding experiments with concept designs, A3 drawings, CAD, code, rough costs and what each result
  would mean. Made with Claude (Anthropic) as a research assistant; AI tools are not listed as authors.
